§ `The regulative rules, run with #TRACE`
-- A DEONTIC value cannot be compared in #ASSERT on the stable binary; each duty is asserted above as a decision function, and the rule is run here.
-- 462.32(4)(b): the peace officer MUST file the report WITHIN 7 (days from the execution of the warrant): filed on day 5 (expected: FULFILLED); on day 7, the last day (FULFILLED); on day 8 (BREACH: not filed within seven days); never filed and the clock runs to day 9 (BREACH)
#TRACE `s 462.32(4)(b) the duty to file the report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `s 462.32(4)(b) prepare the report in Form 5.3 and cause it to be filed with the clerk of the court` AT 5
#TRACE `s 462.32(4)(b) the duty to file the report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `s 462.32(4)(b) prepare the report in Form 5.3 and cause it to be filed with the clerk of the court` AT 7
#TRACE `s 462.32(4)(b) the duty to file the report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `s 462.32(4)(b) prepare the report in Form 5.3 and cause it to be filed with the clerk of the court` AT 8
#TRACE `s 462.32(4)(b) the duty to file the report` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 9)
-- 462.321(4)(c): the same duty, for digital assets
#TRACE `s 462.321(4)(c) the duty to file the report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `s 462.321(4)(c) prepare the report in Form 5.3 and cause it to be filed with the clerk of the court` AT 7
#TRACE `s 462.321(4)(c) the duty to file the report` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 9)
